00:16:59,599 --> 00:17:04,718
I will not parlay, as I have said, with armed men at my gate, nor at all with

209
00:17:04,718 --> 00:17:09,599
the people of the Alvin King, whom I remember with small kindness.

210
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:14,797
In this debate, they have no place. Be gone now, air, our arrows fly. And if

211
00:17:14,797 --> 00:17:18,878
you would speak with me again, first dismiss the Elvish host to the woods

212
00:17:18,878 --> 00:17:25,520
where it belongs, and then return, laying down your arms before you approach the threshold.

213
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:30,000
The elven king is my friend, and he has suckered the people of the lake in their

214
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:35,279
need, though they had no claim but friendship on him, answered Bard. We

215
00:17:35,279 --> 00:17:37,919
will give you time to repent your words.

216
00:17:37,919 --> 00:17:44,240
Gather your wisdom, air we return. Then he departed and went back to the camp.

217
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:48,477
Many hours were passed. The banner bearers returned and trumpeters stood

218
00:17:48,477 --> 00:17:54,718
forth and blew a blast. In the name of Escaroth and the forest, one cried, "We

219
00:17:54,718 --> 00:17:59,759
speak unto Thorenthra's son Oakenshield, calling himself the king under the

220
00:17:59,759 --> 00:18:04,319
mountain, and we bid him consider well the claims that have been urged or be

221
00:18:04,319 --> 00:18:09,439
declared our foe." At the least he shall deliver one 12th portion of the treasure

222
00:18:09,439 --> 00:18:15,279
unto Bard as the dragon slayer and as the heir of Jiren. From that portion

223
00:18:15,279 --> 00:18:19,840
Bard will himself contribute to the aid of Esgar. But if Doran would have the

224
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:24,797
friendship and honor of the lands about, as his sireers had of old, then he will

225
00:18:24,797 --> 00:18:29,840
give also somewhat of his own for the comfort of the men of the lake. Then

226
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:34,878
Thoren seized a bow of horn and shot an arrow at the speaker. it smoked into his

227
00:18:34,878 --> 00:18:37,520
shield and stuck there quivering.

228
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:42,558
Since such is your answer, he called in return, I declare the mountain besieged.

229
00:18:42,558 --> 00:18:46,878
You shall not depart from it until you call on your side for a truce and a

230
00:18:46,878 --> 00:18:52,000
parley. We will bear no weapons against you, but we leave you to your gold. You

231
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:57,119
may eat that if you will." With that, the messengers departed swiftly, and the

232
00:18:57,119 --> 00:19:02,080
dwarves were left to consider their case. So grim had Thoren become that

233
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:06,159
even if they had wished, the others would not have dared to find fault with

234
00:19:06,159 --> 00:19:11,919
him. But indeed most of them seemed to share his mind, except perhaps old fat

235
00:19:11,919 --> 00:19:16,718
Bomber and Feelely and Killy Bilbo, of course, disapproved of the whole turn of

236
00:19:16,718 --> 00:19:21,279
affairs. He had by now had more than enough of the mountain, and being

237
00:19:21,279 --> 00:19:27,200
besieged inside it was not at all to his taste. The whole place still stinks of

238
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:32,558
dragon, he grumbled to himself. And it makes me sick, and Cram is beginning

239
00:19:32,558 --> 00:19:33,000
simply to stick in my throat. Chapter
